<HelloFraandsPage title="Community guidelines" summary="Izzat se baat karein; har insaan ki hadon ka dhyaan rakhein." review={true} related={[{href:'/terms',label:'Terms of use'},{href:'/recording-policy',label:'Recording & consent'},{href:'/grievance',label:'Grievance redressal'}]}>
<p><strong>Preview:</strong> these guidelines describe the planned calling service. Calling, reports, strike enforcement and automated moderation are not active just because they are described here.</p>
<h2>What is welcome</h2>
<p>Adults aged 18 or older can talk, vent, find company or discuss a shared interest. Astrology and tarot are for reflection and entertainment, with no promised outcomes. Respect a person's decision to decline, end or change the topic.</p>
<p>In the <a href="/women-only">women-only lane</a>, everyday health experiences are a normal topic. Discussing periods, PCOS or pregnancy is not in itself sexual misconduct. Harassment is still reportable. Hosts must not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
<h2>What is not allowed</h2>
<ul><li>Sexual or suggestive talk, abuse, threats, harassment or coercion.</li><li>Asking for or sharing phone numbers, social accounts, addresses or private contact details.</li><li>Asking for money, selling services or remedies, or arranging meetings.</li><li>Impersonation, false qualifications, or professional medical, legal or financial advice.</li><li>Using the service under 18, sharing another person's private information or making your own recording of them.</li></ul>
<h2>How planned reports and strikes work</h2>
<p>Hosts will be able to end a call with <strong>*</strong>, or use <strong>#</strong> to end, block the caller from that host and flag an incident. A block stops future contact with that host; it does not by itself prove misconduct or permanently ban an account.</p>
<p>At launch, every recording is planned to go through automated post-call review. Flagged content goes to an administrator for review. A flag or report is pending until reviewed; AI does not independently decide a permanent ban. Mentions of self-harm go to welfare review and must never count as a strike.</p>
<p>The proposed caller policy is a ban after <strong>three confirmed strikes</strong>. Blocking by three distinct hosts is planned to freeze the caller account pending review; two calls ended with the host's # key within 24 hours are planned to trigger a 24-hour suspension. These are planned controls, not a guarantee that harm will be detected.</p>
<p>The specification also proposes forfeiting a banned caller's remaining wallet balance and blocking re-registration with that phone number. Wallet forfeiture remains under legal review; it is not a live preview penalty. Ending a call or making a report alone does not forfeit the wallet. Connected usage remains billable under the planned <a href="/wallet-terms">wallet terms</a>.</p>
<h2>Live moderation comes later</h2>
<p>A later phase proposes an automated warning for a first sexual or abusive detection, then ending the call after a second detection in the same call and sending a pending incident for review. Do not wait for an automated warning before hanging up.</p>
<p>Hosts also follow the <a href="/hosts/rules">host rules</a>. See <a href="/report">Report a user</a> for reporting availability and <a href="/grievance">grievance redressal</a> for the published route to challenge account action. No response time or outcome is promised by this preview.</p>
